# {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared

The Claude Code plugin every **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** repository enables. It ships what the
whole team shares; anything one repository needs alone stays in that repository.

## The sharing rule

| A skill, agent or hook is needed by… | It lives in |
| --- | --- |
| More than one role, or more than one repository | This plugin |
| One code repository only | That repository's own `.claude/` |

Ties go to the code repository. Promoting later is cheap; a shared plugin full of
one-team tools taxes every session of every teammate.

## What's in it

Every skill carries the project name, so that with several projects installed the
`/` menu says which one you are reaching for.

| Skill | Invoke | Does |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context` | `/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context` | Reads the knowledge base before work that depends on project facts |
| `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-knowledge` | `/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-knowledge` | Adds or updates a document in the owning workspace, index and reviewer included |
| `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-links` | `/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-links` | Finds and repairs broken links, bad filenames and misrendering tables |
| `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-space` | `/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-space` | Creates a workspace: folder, README, `CLAUDE.md` with an owner, area-map row |

Decision records are deliberately **not** here: `/tsh-core:managing-decision-records`
already owns that format and lifecycle, and `conventions/decisions.md` matches it. Two
standards for one artifact is how they drift apart.

All four resolve the knowledge base the same way, through
[shared/locating-the-knowledge-base.md](shared/locating-the-knowledge-base.md), so they
work from the context repository, from the project catalog and from any code repository
beside it.

## Enable it in a code repository

The repository sits next to `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/` in the project catalog. Commit
this to its `.claude/settings.json`:

```json
{
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context": {
      "source": { "source": "directory", "path": "../{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context" }
    }
  },
  "enabledPlugins": { "{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared@{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context": true }
}
```

Start Claude Code in the repository, accept the trust dialog, check `/plugin list`.

## Adding a component

Add `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, `agents/<name>.md` or `hooks/hooks.json` — only
`plugin.json` lives inside `.claude-plugin/`. Name a new skill
`{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-<what-it-does>`, matching the four above. Bump `version` in
`.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, add a [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) line, run
`claude plugin validate .` from this folder and from the repository root, then open a
pull request to the repository owner. Teammates pick it up with
`/plugin update {{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared@{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context`; without the bump the
update reaches nobody.
